we're entering the area now in the  crosshairs of russia's territorial  ambitions the heart of the donbass  region in eastern ukraine  it's here that the russians are now  focusing and where there's evidence of  fresh attacks all along our route  as we travel in we see reinforcements  arriving all the time as the ukrainians  send extra troops and military hardware  to fight the russians off  this is one of the latest hits in the  past 24 hours the russians have hit a  volley of strikes in towns like that  moved in eastern ukraine and just 30  kilometers down that road is newly  captured russian territory as they're  trying to claim more and more land in  the donbass region  but the russian bombs are finding new  targets every day the towns around here  are being hit day and night  the targets in the centre of heavily  built up residential areas this was a  factory providing heating for around 10  000 people in the district  there are a number killed in this attack  amongst them a soldier and others who  had a narrow escape  this soldier was in the middle of  sending an audio note to his friend when  the explosion happened  it was a few hundred meters away he  tells us minutes afterwards he's filming  himself with the smoke behind him to the  same friend  what do you think the russians are  trying to  they're targeting civilians he says  they're just trying to make civilians  panic  the ukrainian successes in fighting off  the russians from kievan hakeev has  meant the invaders have upped the tempo  with increased savagery to try to  wrestle control of donbass they haven't  counted on the people here  they may capture territory but they  can't make us ukrainians their slaves  anatoly tells us we'll never sing to the  russian tune it's impossible just  impossible  the residents clear up their shattered  homes with a battle-hardened weariness  now  they've endured nearly three months of  this trauma and turmoil  why should i be afraid she says i just  don't want the things landing in my  house and i don't want them to hit  people  [Music]  but people are dying and families are  suffering terribly  every person who dies at home in their  town or on the battlefield in donbass  like yuri leaves behind broken-hearted  relatives  yuri was 32 years old among the mourners  is his 13 year old daughter darina  another family utterly devastated by  this war  so many of his friends turned out for  his send-off  and saying goodbye never gets any easier  i want to hug you just one more time  she's crying  mothers aren't meant to bury their  children  [Music]  fellow soldiers try to give them the  respect they feel a fallen comrade  deserves  [Applause]  they know there's a chance they'll face  the same fate but they'll leave here to  continue defending donbass anyway  and to those who loved him and will miss  him yuri dies a hero  is it worth it  no alina says no it's not worth his  death  because my child is gone just suddenly  my child's gone and i'm so sad  but he died a hero she goes on  russia may have scaled down its military  ambitions the tactics and focus may have  altered but for those still being killed  and terrorized it doesn't feel much  different  alex crawford sky news in the donbass  region ukraine
 

